From 9c1d6068fbb65ab31220ea9fccaa97d93ddf648c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 06:18:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add "Show more" pagination and search to long lists
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New shared primitives in ui/kit.js — ShowMoreButton and SearchInput
(with a new Search icon) — applied to every screen that renders a
list that can grow unbounded over time, so nobody has to scroll
through months of history or a large client roster:

- AdminPanel: client list (search by name + paginate, 8 at a time)
- TrainerStats: client activity rows (search + paginate)
- BookingAdmin: bookings list (search by client name + paginate,
  resets on tab/search change)
- PackageAdmin: pending/approved packages (search by client name +
  paginate per tab)
- ClientMeasurements: measurement history (paginate only — no
  meaningful search dimension for a single client's own history)
- LiveTraining: past session list (paginate only)
- BookingClient: "Mano rezervacijos" (paginate only — personal list)

Search only shows once a list actually exceeds 8 items, so small
lists stay uncluttered.

Deliberately left untouched: WorkoutPlanBuilder's and WorkoutPresets'
exercise lists (building/arranging a plan needs full visibility) and
the ExercisePicker exercise-database browser (already has its own
search+filter). ProgressPhotos.js and ProgressCompare.js already had
their own "show more" pagination from before this pass.
